 What is Write-Ahead Logging?
Write-Ahead Logging means that SQL Server writes the transaction log records to the transaction log 
before the corresponding modified data pages are written to the data files. 
This ensures that the log contains the information required for recovery in case of a failure.

A transaction can be committed once the required log records have been hardened to the transaction log, 
even though the modified data pages may still be in the buffer pool and written to the data files later.

WAL
→ Protect/recover transaction changes

Checkpoint
→ Flush dirty pages toward data files
→ Helps define/reduce recovery work
